    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d730">

                <pb facs="0817" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/3169: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Third Secretary of Embassy in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wendelin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-09-15T23:00:00+00:00">September 15, 1936—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 16—12:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>150. Department’s telegram No. 125, September 14, 6 p.m. Americans are being
                    informed that Embassy will be closed as a place of refuge Tuesday, September 22,
                    and that those wishing to take advantage of final opportunity to leave Spain
                    will be evacuated from Alicante on the <hi rendition="#italic">Quincy</hi> next
                    Saturday. I have asked <hi rendition="#italic">Quincy</hi> to be at Alicante
                    Saturday morning. Destitute Americans will be evacuated in accordance with
                    instructions Department’s telegram No. 124, September 14, 4 p.m.<anchor n="39"
                        xml:id="d730-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wendelin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d730-f1" n="39" xml:id="d730-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; the Embassy was authorized to draw on $300 Red Cross fund. The
                    amount drawn was $133.79. (352.1115/1455)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
